# The upstream-to-native agreement (docs/spec/endpoints.md §4): the
# native pinned duplex — Poseidon2-16 self-checked against the pinned
# known-answer test, with the pinned duplexing semantics (prefix-free
# absorbs, length binding, LIFO output, output invalidation) — replays the
# checked-in captured upstream verifier transcript and derives every sample the
# upstream verifier derived: all six extension challenges coordinate
# by coordinate, the grinding check, and the four query indices. With
# primitives held fixed by the known-answer check, this validates the
# orchestration-layer semantics — the layer where the weak-Fiat-Shamir
# bug class lives. Scoped evidence about this fixture at this pin, never
# universal conformance.

# RUN: zkc-run --replay-duplex %zkc-replay-fixture | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: duplex replay: 82 events, 29 derived samples, all agree with the captured upstream transcript
